weight:700">Konsa</span><span>&nbsp;at around &pound;60m, and </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;accept they must significantly improve on an initial proposal reported in some quarters at around &pound;30m and in others considerably higher. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Konsa</span><span>&#39;s contract runs to 2028, which is the lever </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;are leaning on. The Guardian reports a second bid is expected. Treat the specific figures as unsettled.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The appeal is obvious and it is not only about </span><span style="font-weight:700">Saliba</span><span>: </span><span style="font-weight:700">Konsa</span><span>&nbsp;plays centre-back and right-back to a high standard, which in a squad missing </span><span style="font-weight:700">Timber</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Copley</span><span>&nbsp;is worth a premium. Whether </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;should pay </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Villa</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&#39;s premium in the third week of August, with the champions&#39; leverage at its lowest, is the argument being had inside and outside the club.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>The alternatives are thinner than the volume of speculation suggests. The Athletic&#39;s </span><span style="font-weight:700">Phil Costa</span><span>&nbsp;reported on August 6 that </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;admire </span><span style="font-weight:700">Cristian Romero</span><span>&nbsp;but that </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Tottenham</span><span>&#39;s refusal to sell to their north London neighbours makes it &quot;a non-starter&quot;; the Argentine has since agreed personal terms with </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Atl&eacute;tico Madrid</span><span>&nbsp;after </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Inter</span><span>&nbsp;had verbally agreed a &euro;40m fee, and a move away from the Premier League looks the likely end point. </span><span style="font-weight:700">John Stones</span><span>, a free agent after leaving </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Manchester City</span><span>&nbsp;and fresh from a strong World Cup, is the cheapest serious option on the board &mdash; </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;are interested, and </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Chelsea</span><span>&nbsp;are competing. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Iv&aacute;n Fresneda</span><span>&nbsp;of </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Sporting CP</span><span>&nbsp;has also been floated as a right-sided option. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Fabrizio Romano</span><span>&nbsp;has said </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;want a centre-back and a winger before the deadline and are &quot;nowhere near done.&quot;</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Ins &amp; Outs &mdash; Summer 2026</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">IN</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Bruno Guimar&atilde;es</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Newcastle United</span><span>, &pound;75m (+&pound;7m to </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Lyon</span><span>), 4yr &middot; </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Aug 8</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Piero Hincapi&eacute;</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Bayer Leverkusen</span><span>, &pound;34.5m, option triggered from loan &middot; </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Jun 25</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Christos Tzolis</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Club Brugge</span><span>, &pound;34m, 5yr &middot; </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Jul 23</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Illan Meslier</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Leeds United</span><span>, free &middot; </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Jul 9</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Elijah Upson</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Tottenham Hotspur</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, free (academy)</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">OUT</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Leandro Trossard</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Be&#351;ikta&#351;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, &pound;15.3m rising to &pound;17m</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Jakub Kiwior</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">FC Porto</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, &pound;14.7m (+&pound;4.2m add-ons), obligation from loan</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Christian N&oslash;rgaard</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Everton</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, &pound;7m</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Karl Hein</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Werder Bremen</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, &pound;2.6m, option triggered</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>Gross spend approx. </span><span style="font-weight:700">&pound;144m</span><span>&nbsp;&middot; income approx. </span><span style="font-weight:700">&pound;40m</span><span>&nbsp;&middot; window closes </span><span style="font-weight:700">11pm, Tuesday September 1</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;(WSL: September 3)</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The Rumour Mill</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">The smaller live threads, the sagas still simmering, and where each of them actually sits on the paper trail.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Myles Lewis-Skelly &mdash; concrete-ish, and contested.</span><span>&nbsp;Football London reported that </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Chelsea</span><span>&nbsp;have been offered the chance to sign the 19-year-old, with The Guardian following. The Athletic&#39;s </span><span style="font-weight:700">James Oberstien</span><span>&nbsp;then reported the opposite reading &mdash; that </span><span style="font-weight:700">Lewis-Skelly</span><span>&nbsp;wants to stay and establish himself &mdash; and </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;sources have said the club is not actively offering him. No fee has been reported. The context is real even if the story is not yet: the midfield just got a &pound;75m more crowded. </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Status: link, disputed.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Gabriel Jesus &mdash; advanced interest.</span><span>&nbsp;With one year left on his contract and a place behind </span><span style="font-weight:700">Gy&ouml;keres</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Havertz</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Merino</span><span>&nbsp;in the pecking order, </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Napoli</span><span>&nbsp;have made contact with his camp and </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Al-Ahli</span><span>&nbsp;retain interest. </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;have set an asking price reported at &pound;17m-&pound;20m and want a permanent deal; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Napoli</span><span>&nbsp;have been weighing something closer to &euro;20m. Wages remain the obstacle. CaughtOffside reported on August 11 that </span><span style="font-weight:700">Jesus</span><span>&nbsp;is open to it. There is a real chance he simply sees out the year and leaves free. </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Status: concrete interest, no agreement.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Reiss Nelson &mdash; talks.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">West Ham United</span><span>, now a Championship club after relegation, are in discussions over the 26-year-old, with </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Benfica</span><span>&nbsp;also credited with interest. Loans at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Fulham</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Brentford</span><span>&nbsp;across the last two seasons produced 26 appearances and nine starts. A permanent exit is overdue for both parties. </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Status: talks.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Ethan Nwaneri &mdash; sounded out.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">AC Milan</span><span>, </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Borussia Dortmund</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">RB Leipzig</span><span>&nbsp;have all been credited with interest after an underwhelming loan at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Marseille</span><span>. </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;would want a buy-back clause in any permanent sale. He scored against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Dortmund</span><span>&nbsp;on Saturday, which does not hurt his price. </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Status: interest.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">F&aacute;bio Vieira &mdash; stalled.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Hamburger SV</span><span>&nbsp;want him but their &euro;20m option to buy, carried over from the loan, is beyond their means. </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;must decide whether to take less or wait for another bidder. </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Status: stalled.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Tommy Setford &mdash; loan sought.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">UD Las Palmas</span><span>&nbsp;are pursuing a loan for the young goalkeeper. With </span><span style="font-weight:700">Meslier</span><span>&nbsp;arriving behind </span><span style="font-weight:700">Raya</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Kepa</span><span>, a season of senior football abroad makes sense. </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Status: interest.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="font-weight:700">Unconfirmed and worth flagging:</span><span>&nbsp;a report on Wednesday claimed a European club has &quot;submitted an official offer&quot; for an </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;duo; the item traces to CaughtOffside citing a journalist and has not been corroborated by a tier-one source. We are not naming players on that basis. Equally, several widely circulated &quot;gossip&quot; items linking </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;to </span><span style="font-weight:700">Kingsley Coman</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Viktor Tsygankov</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Benjamin &Scaron;e&scaron;ko</span><span>&nbsp;trace back to columns from previous seasons and are not live. </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Status: unverified / stale.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700;text-decoration:n